b/dev is a staging tree that Pat revises freely, so work built on it
must be revised or abandoned whenever a commit beneath it changes,
and a series posted against it cannot be applied to trunk as sent.
This series makes trunk the base for contributor work. Work that
needs something only on b/dev and cannot be done on trunk is not
ready; the contributor says so and waits for it to land.

Patch 1 replaces the CLAUDE.md paragraph that permitted basing work
on b/dev. It supersedes "[PATCH] claude: Fix a typo in the b/dev
guidance" [1], which fixed a typo in the paragraph removed here.

Patch 2 says the same in the lab-process-mail prompt, where a pass
reads b/dev as a source. LAB_BASE_BRANCH stays, since it serves an
operator whose own assistant should see the tree as they do; its
default is already trunk().

